<!DOCTYPE html>
{#
  Admin-backend login 2FA code e-mail. Sent from AuthService::sendCodeEmail() (login purpose
  only -- password-reset codes and the password-changed notice stay plain text for now) via a
  TemplatedEmail (htmlTemplate + textTemplate, see login_code.txt.twig). Built on the canonical
  bulletproof-table structure documented in VeloWetzikon_Design_Tokens/design-system/email.html /
  email-template.html -- same trimmed-to-what-this-email-needs approach as
  report_confirmation.html.twig (paragraphs, a code block instead of a button, footer). Keep both
  in sync if the template's structure changes; don't let this drift into its own one-off pattern.

  No UTM parameters on the logo/Impressum links here, unlike report_confirmation.html.twig -- UTM
  tracks public-campaign engagement (utm_campaign=meldung_bestaetigung etc.), which doesn't apply
  to a transactional code sent to an already-known admin logging into the backend.

  Logo URL: {{ absolute_url(asset(...)) }}, not a config parameter -- requestLoginChallenge() (and
  therefore this e-mail) only ever runs inside the POST /auth/login HTTP request, so the current
  request's own scheme+host is already correct, same reasoning as report_confirmation.html.twig.
#}
<html lang="de" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:v="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:vml" xmlns:o="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<meta http-equiv="X-UA-Compatible" content="IE=edge">
<meta name="color-scheme" content="light">
<meta name="supported-color-schemes" content="light">
<title>Velofreundliches Wetzikon</title>
<!--[if mso]>
<noscript>
<xml>
<o:OfficeDocumentSettings>
<o:PixelsPerInch>96</o:PixelsPerInch>
</o:OfficeDocumentSettings>
</xml>
</noscript>
<style>
  table { border-collapse: collapse; }
  td, a, body { font-family: Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif !important; }
</style>
<![endif]-->
<style>
  body, table, td, a { -webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; }
  table, td { mso-table-lspace: 0pt; mso-table-rspace: 0pt; }
  img { -ms-interpolation-mode: bicubic; border: 0; height: auto; line-height: 100%; outline: none; text-decoration: none; }
  body { margin: 0; padding: 0; width: 100% !important; background: #fafaf8; }
  a { color: #dc3406; }
  @media screen and (max-width: 600px) {
    .email-container { width: 100% !important; }
    .email-padded { padding-left: 20px !important; padding-right: 20px !important; }
  }
</style>
</head>
<body style="margin:0;padding:0;background:#fafaf8;">

<div style="display:none;max-height:0;overflow:hidden;mso-hide:all;font-size:1px;line-height:1px;color:#fafaf8;">
  {#- Tells the reader something the subject doesn't: the code itself, so it's glanceable from a
      notification/inbox-list preview without opening the e-mail. #}
  Dein Anmeldecode: {{ code }}
</div>

<center style="width:100%;background:#fafaf8;">
<!--[if mso]>
<table role="presentation" width="600" align="center" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0"><tr><td>
<![endif]-->
<table role="presentation" class="email-container" align="center" width="600" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" style="margin:0 auto;max-width:600px;width:100%;">

  <tr>
    <!-- Left/right 41px, not 40px -- matches the card's own content inset exactly: 1px border +
         40px padding on the card below, so the logo and the body text line up on the same left
         edge instead of sitting 9px apart. -->
    <td class="email-padded" style="padding:32px 41px 24px;" align="left">
      <a href="https://velofreundliches-wetzikon.ch/" target="_blank">
        <img src="{{ absolute_url(asset('assets/email/logo.png')) }}" width="168" height="29" alt="Velofreundliches Wetzikon" style="display:block;border:0;outline:none;text-decoration:none;max-width:168px;" />
      </a>
    </td>
  </tr>

  <tr>
    <td style="background:#ffffff;border:1px solid #e8e6e0;border-radius:8px;">
      <table role="presentation" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0">
        <tr>
          <td class="email-padded" style="padding:40px 40px 32px;">

            <p style="margin:0 0 16px;font-family:Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:1.6;color:#000000;">
              Hallo {{ name }},
            </p>
            <p style="margin:0 0 24px;font-family:Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:1.6;color:#000000;">
              mit diesem Code schliesst du die Anmeldung im Backend von Velofreundliches Wetzikon ab:
            </p>

            <!-- Code block -- no button/link to click here (the code is typed into the already-open
                 verify page), so a plain bordered/tinted box standing in for the button slot,
                 same card chrome (#e8e6e0 border, 8px radius) as the outer card itself. -->
            <table role="presentation" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" style="margin:0 0 24px;">
              <tr>
                <td align="center" style="background:#fafaf8;border:1px solid #e8e6e0;border-radius:8px;padding:20px;">
                  <span style="font-family:Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:32px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:10px;color:#000000;">{{ code }}</span>
                </td>
              </tr>
            </table>

            <p style="margin:0 0 24px;font-family:Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px;line-height:1.6;color:#5e5e5a;">
              Der Code ist {{ ttlMinutes }} Minuten gültig. Falls du das nicht warst, kannst du diese E-Mail ignorieren &ndash; ohne den Code kann sich niemand anmelden.
            </p>

            <p style="margin:0;font-family:Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:1.6;color:#000000;">
              Dein Team von<br>Velofreundliches Wetzikon
            </p>

          </td>
        </tr>
      </table>
    </td>
  </tr>

  <tr>
    <td class="email-padded" style="padding:24px 32px 40px;text-align:center;font-family:Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:12px;line-height:1.6;color:#8a8a86;">
      Velofreundliches Wetzikon &mdash; private Initiative<br>
      Thom Hoffmann &middot; Messikommerstrasse 37 &middot; 8620 Wetzikon<br>
      <a href="https://velofreundliches-wetzikon.ch/impressum-editor/" style="color:#8a8a86;text-decoration:underline;">Impressum</a>
    </td>
  </tr>

</table>
<!--[if mso]></td></tr></table><![endif]-->
</center>
</body>
</html>
